{
    "background_story": "Dominic was a renowned scholar of ancient languages, with a particular fascination for Avestan, the sacred tongue of the Zoroastrians. Growing up in a family of linguists, he was exposed to the intricacies of language from a young age. Dominic's passion for Avestan led him to spend years studying the Gathas, the hymns of the prophet Zarathustra. He became an expert in deciphering the complexities of the Avestan script and was soon sought after by museums and universities for his expertise. Dominic's groundbreaking research shed new light on the history of the Zoroastrian faith, and his translations of the Avestan texts are still widely used today. His dedication to the study of Avestan earned him the nickname 'The Keeper of the Sacred Tongue' among his peers.",
